Subject: Cantor llama.cpp Tool Reflection Probe

Description: The minimum falsification experiment proving or rejecting whether an unmodified llama.cpp server can emit a structured Cantor tool call, receive a deterministic semantic expression, import it through a subsequent inference call, and preserve equivalent intended meaning across verbose, condensed, and directive forms.

& [ProbeIdentity] is the bounded provider experiment
  + [specification_uuid] is 93bcb4be-e3a0-4ace-9519-375768597049
  + [solution_uuid] is f12c48dd-0887-4553-9566-e4fba1f0d864
  + [provider] is official ggml-org llama.cpp llama-server
  + [provider_version] is pinned release b10181
  + [provider_interface] is OpenAI-compatible POST /v1/chat/completions with tool calls and JSON-schema response
  + [model] is local gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf unless its embedded chat template cannot perform the probe
  + [host] is a small safe-Rust experiment executable
  + [tool] is cantor_reflect
  + [scope] is one ambiguous term, one purpose, three expression styles, and one normalized result contract
  = must: remain isolated from the authoritative Cantor core
  = must: treat any failure as useful evidence rather than repair it through unbounded prompting

& [ProbeSubject] is the controlled semantic ambiguity
  + [term] is bank
  + [purpose] is decide where to deposit a paycheck
  + [intended_identity] is financial_institution
  + [excluded_identity] is river_bank
  + [next_action] is compare_account_options
  = rationale: the fixture is small, verifiable, and requires contextual identity discrimination

| [ExpressionStyle] is (verbose | condensed | directive)

& [CantorReflectInput] is the model-generated tool argument contract
  + [subject] is bank
  + [purpose] is decide where to deposit a paycheck
  + [expression_style] is one ExpressionStyle requested by the fixture
  = must: reject missing, malformed, extra, or semantically changed arguments

& [CantorReflectOutput] is the deterministic host-generated semantic expression
  + [expression_style] is the requested ExpressionStyle
  + [semantic_expression] is a style-specific articulation of intended identity, excluded identity, purpose, and next action
  + [source_address] is fixture://bank/paycheck-deposit
  + [authority] is test_fixture_only
  = must: vary surface organization while preserving identical normalized meaning
  - never: call another model to synthesize the tool result

& [InferenceImportResult] is the schema-constrained second-pass result
  + [selected_identity] is financial_institution
  + [excluded_identity] is river_bank
  + [purpose] is decide where to deposit a paycheck
  + [next_action] is compare_account_options
  + [expression_style] is the style actually imported
  + [source_address] is fixture://bank/paycheck-deposit
  = must: be produced by the model after the tool result enters message history
  = must: be parsed and validated independently by the Rust host

& [CheckpointedProbeCycle] is one expression-style trial
  + [step_1_request] is send system instruction, user request, tool schema, and forced relevant style
  + [step_2_parse] is require exactly one cantor_reflect tool call
  + [step_3_validate] is validate tool name and CantorReflectInput before executing the fixture
  + [step_4_reflect] is return the deterministic CantorReflectOutput
  + [step_5_continue] is append the assistant tool call and tool result to a second chat-completion request
  + [step_6_import] is require an InferenceImportResult through JSON-schema constrained output
  + [step_7_compare] is validate normalized meaning and compare it with the other expression styles
  + [step_8_record] is emit sanitized requests, tool call, tool result, final result, token usage, timings, and faults
  = must: exclude provider-private reasoning content from the durable trace

& [AcceptanceSet] is the minimum pass condition
  + [LTP-001] is llama-server advertises a usable chat template and responds on localhost
  + [LTP-002] is each style produces exactly one parseable cantor_reflect call
  + [LTP-003] is each tool call preserves the exact subject, purpose, and requested style
  + [LTP-004] is the host returns three different surface expressions with one normalized meaning
  + [LTP-005] is each second inference imports the expression into the required normalized result
  + [LTP-006] is all three normalized results are semantically equal
  + [LTP-007] is the trace distinguishes model output, deterministic tool output, validation, usage, timing, and failure
  + [LTP-008] is rerunning the probe preserves the contract even when wording varies

& [FaultSet] is the required negative evidence
  + [server_unavailable] is llama-server cannot be reached
  + [template_unsupported] is tool schema is not rendered or parsed correctly
  + [tool_not_called] is the model answers directly or emits no call
  + [wrong_tool] is any tool other than cantor_reflect
  + [argument_fault] is malformed or semantically incorrect tool parameters
  + [tool_loop] is the second pass calls the tool again instead of importing the result
  + [schema_fault] is the final content is not valid InferenceImportResult
  + [semantic_fault] is any normalized field changes across styles
  + [provider_fault] is timeout, context overflow, refusal, malformed response, or process failure
  = must: fail visibly and preserve sanitized evidence

& [ImplementationBoundary] is the anti-expansion rule
  + [inside] is pinned llama.cpp installation metadata, local server launcher, Rust HTTP tool-loop harness, deterministic fixture, validation, and sanitized trace
  + [outside] is SOP parser, database, neural router, Faculty runtime, NarrativeCantor, distributed agents, hidden states, KV transport, model training, and external effects
  = must: complete or reject this probe before adding another Cantor tool

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the tool-reflection probe justification record
  + [fold_1_subject] is minimum llama.cpp tool call that returns alternative semantic expressions for import into a later inference checkpoint
  + [fold_2_boundary] is structured tool parameters, deterministic reflection, second-pass semantic import, and equivalence inside; full Cantor and provider modification outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is trial, style, tool call, arguments, expression, source address, normalized import result, usage, timing, and fault
  + [fold_4_governance] is localhost binding, pinned provider, exact validation, test-only authority, sanitized traces, no private reasoning, and visible failure
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is request, parse, validate, reflect, continue, import, compare, and record
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is unsupported template, direct answer, malformed arguments, tool loop, schema failure, semantic drift, prompt overfitting, and provider failure
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is one isolated falsification probe authorized without reactivating deferred Cantor architecture

